# NovaGram: theme assets are data, not source - never translate their line
# endings on checkout.
#
# The colours of every built-in theme except the default light one come from
# these files. Theme.getThemeFileValues() splits them into lines and hands each
# value to Utilities.parseInt(), which takes the terminating character along
# with the digits; Integer.parseInt("-1\r") then throws, the exception is
# swallowed, and the colour becomes 0. The result is a dark theme where every
# background is black and every piece of text is transparent.
#
# Upstream used to guard against exactly this with a BuildConfig
# .BUILD_HOST_IS_WINDOWS branch in parseInt that matched the number with a
# regex. 12.10.0 removed both the branch and the flag, so on a Windows checkout
# with core.autocrlf=true nothing stands between the assets and the parser.
*.attheme -text
